A||||6||mrfiero||New shoes for my baby!||||10||
Z||000000||mrfiero||08-21-2001||09:43 PM||||I finally located a set of original GT+4 tires for my 16K mile '88 GT!  What a pain.  I was lucky enough to find a set of rears (215/60) from a list member and even luckier to find the fronts (205/60) at (of all places) a Goodyear dealer.  Go figure!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>He was able to find 2 of them at the local Denver warehouse......I am searching for more, but I'm happy to have this set.  Now I'm good for another 10 years or so.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>BTW.......I am considering installing a set of lowered springs too.  It needs new shocks & struts anyways and adding lowered springs wouldn't be too much extra work.  Any opinions?  <P>I have used lowered springs before, so that's not what's at issue here......I've always prided my GT for the fact that it was 100% original.  Now that I'm replacing tires and shocks (and installing a factory subwoofer) should I say "what the heck?" and do it?  <P>The only reason I am considering this is I have always hated the way a stock '88 Fiero sits......it's too high (too much of a wheelwell gap).  The lowered springs would make it look soooo much better, but will "alter" it from "stock".<P>Any comments or suggestions???<P>Thanks.     <P>   ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Galen||08-21-2001||09:46 PM||||You're car, make it so that you enjoy it. Dont worry about others. cars are built to be used and abused..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||08-21-2001||09:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>You're car, make it so that you enjoy it. Dont worry about others. cars are built to be used and abused..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know......I still won't drive it much, but at least when I do I'll be happy with how it looks.  <P>I will more than likely go ahead and lower it.......I can always reinstall the factory springs if/when I ever sell it (not likely to sell it anytime soon!).   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||08-21-2001||10:09 PM||||Well, for a low mileage original - especially one you've gone to the trouble of finding original tires for - I'd leave it exactly as stock.  Fieros are cheap if you want one to play with and modify.  Original low-mileage cars are a rarity, and yes, owning one, IMO, entails an obligation to the car.<P>Do what you want, but any car can be restored.  They are only original once.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hank is Here||08-21-2001||10:38 PM||||Well, lowering the car is not a harmful or permanent mod, it can be undone in a day.  Personally I would not do it but to each his own||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||08-21-2001||10:49 PM||||Put the lowering springs on.  Then you can have the original springs cleaned up and powdercoated so they'll look ever better if you ever decide to sell the car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||08-22-2001||10:36 AM||||What he said, this is NOT a perminant change.  And I agree, they did the 88s' ride height wrong :)(<P>]<BR>] <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>Put the lowering springs on.  Then you can have the original springs cleaned up and powdercoated so they'll look ever better if you ever decide to sell the car  :)<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
